        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "0fa108cb-f3aa-535c-a5d6-bb6aa86f628d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Singapore, North America, South Korea\n- Buildings: Tanjong Pagar Centre, UOB Plaza, One Raffles Place, Republic Plaza, 63 Building, Bank of China Tower\n- Topics: tallest buildings, height records\n\nFacts:\n- One Raffles Place was completed in 1986 at 280 m.\n- At the time of its completion in 1986, One Raffles Place was the tallest building in the world outside North America.\n- One Raffles Place surpassed South Korea's 63 Building, which had been completed one year earlier.\n- Bank of China Tower later succeeded One Raffles Place as the tallest building in the world outside North America.\n- UOB Plaza, One Raffles Place, and Republic Plaza jointly held Singapore's tallest-building record for over 20 years.\n- Tanjong Pagar Centre is 290 m tall.\n- Tanjong Pagar Centre currently holds the title of tallest building in Singapore.\n- Tanjong Pagar Centre broke the Singapore height record previously held jointly by UOB Plaza, One Raffles Place, and Republic Plaza.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "3a741063-cb35-5a27-a87b-e0024b6ff491",
        "text": "Page: Tanjong Pagar Centre. Sentence: With a height of 290 m , it is currently the tallest building in Singapore, breaking the record held jointly by UOB Plaza, One Raffles Place and Republic Plaza for over 20 years.\nPage: One Raffles Place. Sentence: At 280 m , it was also the tallest building in the world outside North America at the time of its completion in 1986, surpassing South Korea's 63 Building completed one year earlier, until it was succeeded by the Bank of China Tower.\nPage: List of tallest buildings in Singapore. Sentence: Tanjong Pagar Centre currently holds the title of tallest building in Singapore.",
